# Tests for PostIncCombiner::chainingForcesExtraCursor.
# A cursor is a pointer register that a group of memory ops walk with
# post-increments. An extra cursor is a second pointer that must stay live
# for a separate advance of the same loop base, which costs a copy of the
# PHI every iteration.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prefer offset loads: the root is a loop PHI advanced by an add.2d that is
# not part of the chain, so the chain can be dropped and each load rebased
# onto the root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
